ig impact on the stock we had a  cost structure that was based on we're  about to get to profitability on a  business that was four times bigger than  what it got shrunk to in the pandemic  and now we've taken our way back up got  into profitability and I'm confident as  we get through these recessionary  pressures That Wall Street will will fix  that the shape of that chart and  and going into a potentially tougher  economic environment which you guys have  already been wrestling with yeah a lot  of tech companies at the start of the  pandemic had a had a great ride you know  whether it was Zoom or Google or others  the pandemic meant a lot of people  working inside and using their products  that was not the case for us and so I  would say what's coming is actually  maybe the the third or fourth hardest  thing we've faced in terms of the coming  potential recession or the recession  that we're already in so we're ready we  have a strong team and frankly on you  know with a two-sided Marketplace on the  driver's side typically there are more  drivers looking for work in a recession  but what about on the demand side I mean  how are you seeing like higher inflation  if you look back at  inflation affects us mostly on insurance  if you look back you've added a fee for  now right uh our service fee has gone up  related to insurance if you look back at  recessions and you look at  transportation ground transportation  specifically it stays pretty static so  perhaps growth slows down in a recession  but people need to get around and so I'm  less concerned you know than if I was uh  to knock on our competitor you know in  the food delivery business in a  recession you know getting a 30 salad is  probably going to be less likely some  someone does in a recession than uh in a  pandemic but just coming back to Wall  Street and if you look back at this  chart I mean the Market's looking at it  thank you the Mark is seeming a lot more  confident and Uber's more Diversified  ye