at when it  comes to Market it will need to happen  on existing Transportation Network  the idea is we're going to have a hybrid  Network where the far majority of rides  for a very long time will be with  because I was wrong we'll be with human  drivers but over time you know let's say  10 percent of rides happen with an  autonomous vehicle in three years that's  not a prediction it's just hypothetical  and in three years ten percent then go  three years after that goes to 20 you'll  always as a customer want to be on a  network where you can always get a ride  I'm going to have to pause you because  my clock is up thank you so much thank  you  and that's it for today's Tech news  briefing for more coverage of this  year's Tech live conference visit our  website  wsj.com I'm Zoe Thomas for The Wall  Street Journal  thanks for listening  [Music]  [Music]

